commit 27168608
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 12:10:05 -0600
subject: feat(routing): full model catalog in pickers, smart-router model subset, per-model fallbacks

Three user-requested capabilities:

1. ModelSelectModal now shows the FULL 9Router catalog — every registered
   provider's models, connected or not (previously only CONNECTED providers
   appeared, so a fresh install showed just the mock/no-auth providers).
   Unconnected providers get an amber "not connected" badge. Works for
   combos, capacity adapter (vision/audio) and judge pickers alike.

2. Smart Router "Allowed models" subset: settings.smartRouter.allowedModels
   restricts the router to explicit "provider/model" strings or wildcard
   patterns ("openai/*", "*/claude-*"). Complements allowedProviders. New
   input + help text in the Smart Router card.

3. Per-Model / Per-Provider Fallbacks (settings.modelFallbacks): attach an
   ordered fallback chain directly to an exact model ("openai/gpt-4o") or
   an entire provider ("openai") — single-model requests route through the
   combo engine automatically when the target fails. Composes with combos
   (combos unchanged); guard prevents infinite recursion. New "Per-Model /
   Per-Provider Fallbacks" card on /dashboard/combos with a line-editor UI
   (target:fallback1,fallback2 per line).

Tests: unit/model-fallbacks.test.js (4: exact-model chain, provider-level
chain, no-wrap when unset, dedupe) + smart-router-resolve.test.js extended
with allowedModels wildcard + no-match cases (7 total). Full suite: 1691
passed / 88 failed (pre-existing baseline only).

Part of: Smart Router & Fallback UX plan (Phase 2/3)


